Here is a simple JavaScript function that finds the longest word in a sentence:

```javascript
function findLongestWord(sentence) {
    var words = sentence.split(' ');
    var longestWord = '';

    for(var i = 0; i < words.length; i++){
        if(words[i].length > longestWord.length){
            longestWord = words[i];
        }
    }

    return longestWord;
}
```

This function works by splitting the input sentence into an array of words, then looping through this array to find the longest word. The `split` method splits a string into an array of substrings based on a specified delimiter (in this case, a space character), and returns the new array.

In the loop, we check if the length of the current word is greater than the length of the currently stored longest word. If it is, we replace the longest word with the current one. After checking all the words, we return the longest one found.

