    private double length;
    private double width;

    // Constructor
    public Rectangle(double length, double width) {
        this.length = length;
        this.width = width;
    }

    // Method to calculate area
    public double getArea() {
        return this.length * this.width;
    }

    // Method to calculate perimeter
    public double getPerimeter() {
        return 2 * (this.length + this.width);
    }

    // Method to compare two rectangles based on their areas
    public static int compare(Rectangle r1, Rectangle r2) {
        double area1 = r1.getArea();
        double area2 = r2.getArea();

        if(area1 > area2)
            return 1;
        else if(area1 < area2)
            return -1;
        else 
            return 0;   
    }
}
```

In this class, we have defined two instance variables `length` and `width`. The constructor `Rectangle()` initializes these variables. 

The method `getArea()` returns the area of the rectangle by multiplying length and width.

The method `getPerimeter()` calculates the perimeter of the rectangle which is twice the sum of length and width.

The `compare()` method compares the areas of two rectangles. It takes two `Rectangle` objects as parameters, computes their areas using the `getArea()` method, and then compares them. If the area of the first rectangle is greater than the second one, it returns 1. If the area of the first rectangle is less than the second one, it returns -1. If both areas are equal, it returns 0.

